18. REVENUE GENERATION AND MONETISATION STRATEGY
18.1 Revenue Generation Overview
Interlink will adopt a hybrid revenue generation model designed to ensure financial sustainability while keeping professional mentorship affordable and accessible.
The platform will not depend solely on mentees paying mentors. Instead, Interlink will generate income through mentorship transaction commissions, premium subscriptions, career development services, corporate mentorship programmes, institutional partnerships, and sponsored mentorship initiatives.
The business model will be built around three key stakeholders:
Mentors
Share professional knowledge, experience, and expertise.
Earn income from paid mentorship sessions.
Build professional credibility and visibility.
Have the option to provide free mentorship.
Mentees
Access experienced professionals.
Pay affordable fees for selected mentorship services.
Access free mentorship opportunities.
Subscribe to optional premium career development features.
Interlink
Facilitates mentor-mentee connections.
Manages mentorship bookings and payments.
Provides the digital infrastructure.
Earns commissions and subscription revenue.
Generates additional income through partnerships and professional development services.
The central business principle is:
Mentors are rewarded for sharing knowledge, mentees receive affordable professional guidance, and Interlink generates sustainable revenue by facilitating meaningful mentorship experiences.
18.2 Primary Revenue Model: Mentor-Earns, Mentee-Contributes
Interlink's primary transaction-based revenue model will allow mentors to offer free or paid mentorship sessions.
Mentors will be able to establish their own session prices within platform guidelines.
For paid mentorship sessions:
The mentor sets a session price.
The mentee selects an available session.
The mentee makes payment through Interlink.
Interlink records the transaction and applicable platform commission.
The mentorship session takes place.
Following successful completion and the applicable dispute period, the mentor receives their earnings.
Interlink retains its commission.
Interlink will initially propose an 85% mentor earnings and 15% platform commission arrangement.
