18.3 Free and Paid Mentorship Options
Interlink will support three mentorship participation models.
A. Free Mentorship
Mentors can voluntarily offer free sessions to support students, graduates, and individuals who may not be able to afford paid mentorship.
Requirements:
Mentors can designate sessions as free.
Mentees can discover free mentorship opportunities.
Free sessions do not attract a platform commission.
Free sessions must follow the same scheduling and community guidelines as paid sessions.
B. Affordable Paid Mentorship
Mentors can offer paid sessions at affordable rates.
Requirements:
Mentors can set session prices within platform guidelines.
Mentees must see the session price before booking.
The platform commission must be disclosed.
Mentor earnings must be displayed before booking confirmation.
Payments must be recorded and reconciled.
C. Premium Mentorship
Experienced professionals can offer specialised mentorship at higher prices.
Examples include:
Executive mentorship.
Business strategy mentorship.
Entrepreneurship guidance.
Leadership development.
Specialist career coaching.
Advanced technical mentorship.
The platform will apply the same commission structure unless an alternative commercial agreement has been approved.
