18.5 Payment Management and Financial Requirements
Payment Processing
Interlink will integrate a suitable payment provider to support online transactions.
Potential providers include:
Paystack.
Flutterwave.
Stripe, where supported and appropriate for the operating market.
The selected provider must support the required payment methods, transaction verification, refunds, settlement, and applicable payout arrangements.
Payment Workflow
Mentee selects a paid mentorship session.
Platform displays session price, platform commission arrangement, and applicable charges.
Mentee confirms booking and initiates payment.
Payment provider processes the transaction.
Backend verifies payment through a trusted provider response or signed webhook.
Booking is confirmed after successful payment verification.
Transaction is recorded in the Interlink financial ledger.
Mentor conducts the session.
Session is marked completed.
The applicable dispute window is observed.
Mentor payout is initiated.
Platform commission is recognised as earned revenue.
Payment confirmation must never rely solely on the frontend redirect or a client-submitted success message.
Mentor Payout Requirements
Mentors must provide valid payout details.
Payout details must be protected.
Mentor earnings must be visible in their dashboard.
Pending, available, paid, and reversed earnings must be distinguishable.
Payout transactions must be recorded.
Failed payouts must be retriable through controlled administrative procedures.
All payouts must reconcile with provider settlement records.
The platform should use a payment provider's supported marketplace or split-settlement capabilities where appropriate. It must not claim to provide regulated escrow services without the necessary provider and regulatory arrangements.
Cancellation and Refund Policy
The platform must define:
Mentor cancellation rules.
Mentee cancellation rules.
Rescheduling conditions.
No-show procedures.
Partial and full refund conditions.
Dispute submission deadlines.
Refund processing procedures.
Refunds and chargebacks must be reflected accurately in the financial ledger and revenue reports.
