Initial Commercial Targets
These are proposed targets to be validated after launch.
Platform commission: 15% of eligible completed paid sessions.
Mentor revenue share: 85% before any separately disclosed deductions.
Payment success rate: At least 95%.
Mentor payout completion: At least 95% of payouts due processed within the defined payout service level.
Refund rate: Monitor and establish a baseline during the first three months.
Repeat booking rate: Establish an initial baseline and improve it quarterly.
Subscription conversion: Measure after premium subscriptions launch.
Corporate and institutional revenue: Establish targets when these services become commercially available.
Revenue Reporting Principle
Interlink must distinguish between:
Gross Transaction Value: The total amount paid by mentees.
Mentor Earnings: The share payable to mentors.
Platform Commission: Interlink's agreed share of eligible transactions.
Net Platform Revenue: Revenue remaining after applicable refunds, discounts, and transaction-related deductions, using the platform's adopted accounting policy.
This distinction is essential for accurate financial reporting and business decision-making.

