Core Financial Relationships
One mentor can offer multiple mentorship services.
One mentorship service can have multiple bookings.
One booking can have associated payment records, including permitted retry attempts.
One successful payment can generate commission and mentor earnings records.
One mentor can receive multiple payouts.
One payment can have one or more refund records where partial refunds are supported.
One user can have multiple subscription records over time.
One subscription belongs to one subscription plan.
One sponsor can fund multiple sponsored programmes.
One sponsored programme can have multiple beneficiary allocations.
Financial Data Integrity Requirements
All monetary amounts must be stored using appropriate fixed-precision decimal types or integer minor units, never floating-point arithmetic.
Every transaction must have a unique internal and provider reference.
Payment provider webhooks must be authenticated and processed idempotently.
A booking must not be paid twice without an explicit additional payment record.
Refunds must reference the original payment.
Mentor earnings must not be released twice.
Financial records must be retained according to applicable legal and accounting requirements.
Administrative adjustments must be traceable.

