25. FINAL MONETISATION DECISION
Interlink will launch with a transaction-based mentorship business model supported by free mentorship opportunities.
The proposed initial commercial arrangement is:
Free mentorship remains available.
Mentors can set prices for paid sessions.
Mentees pay for selected paid sessions.
Mentors receive 85% of eligible completed session revenue.
Interlink retains a proposed 15% commission.
Payments and mentor earnings are managed through the platform.
Optional subscriptions and additional commercial services are introduced progressively.
The platform will initially prioritise individual mentor-mentee transactions, followed by subscriptions, career development services, corporate partnerships, institutional programmes, and sponsored mentorship.
This approach enables Interlink to test its revenue model without making mentorship inaccessible to its target audience.
Core Business Principle:
Interlink creates a platform where professional experience becomes an opportunity to earn, career ambition gains access to guidance, and meaningful connections generate sustainable business value.
INTERLINK — Empowerment. Growth. Connection.

